@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`

-- Tests for il-interpretation-law.l4.
-- Expected values were decided from the words of each section before the module was run. A failing assertion
-- is a finding: none was edited to match the code.

§ `Tests: the other computable provisions`

§§ `Law s 32, with s 21: when the Law began to bind`

#ASSERT `s 32 — the day the Interpretation Law commenced` EQUALS YMD 1981 10 1
#ASSERT (`s 32, s 21 — the moment the Interpretation Law began to bind`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 1981 10 1
#ASSERT (`s 32, s 21 — the moment the Interpretation Law began to bind`)'s `hour` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`s 32, s 21 — the moment the Interpretation Law began to bind`)'s `minute` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 1981 10 1) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0) `is one at which a statute commencing on` `s 32 — the day the Interpretation Law commenced` `binds`
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the moment` (`the moment on` (YMD 1981 10 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59) `is one at which a statute commencing on` `s 32 — the day the Interpretation Law commenced` `binds`

§§ `Law s 1: the Law governs unless another provision or the context says otherwise`

#ASSERT `s 1 — the Law governs` (`The matter in question` WITH `another provision deals with it` IS FALSE, `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the Law governs` (`The matter in question` WITH `another provision deals with it` IS TRUE, `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the Law governs` (`The matter in question` WITH `another provision deals with it` IS FALSE, `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the Law governs` (`The matter in question` WITH `another provision deals with it` IS TRUE, `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law` IS TRUE)

§§ `Law s 1: an enactment given before the Law commenced`

#ASSERT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` (YMD 1981 9 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` (YMD 1981 10 2)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` (YMD 1990 1 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` (YMD 1981 10 1) BECAUSE "a day-level date cannot say whether an enactment given on the day the Law commenced was given before 00:01 on that day"

-- With a moment, the commencement day is settled: before 00:01:00 is before the Law; 00:01:00 itself is not.
#ASSERT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given at` (`the moment on` (YMD 1981 10 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59)
#ASSERT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given at` (`the moment on` (YMD 1981 9 30) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given at` (`the moment on` (YMD 1981 10 1) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given at` (`the moment on` (YMD 1981 10 1) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0)

-- s 3 applies to the words of a later enactment; to an earlier one only for חטא, עוון, פשע, fiscal year and coastal waters.
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1990 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word day` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1990 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word month` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word day` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word fiscal year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word מימי חופין` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word חטא` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word עוון` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word פשע` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1)

-- On the day the Law commenced, the four words s 3 always reaches still answer; the others cannot at day level.
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word fiscal year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1981 10 1)
#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word פשע` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1981 10 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1981 10 1)

-- What the Ordinance text still defines.
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance text still defines` `the word month`
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance text still defines` `the word year`
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance text still defines` `the word day`
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance text still defines` `the word fiscal year`
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance text still defines` `the word מימי חופין`

-- Which definition governs.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1990 1 1) EQUALS `the definition in section 3 of the Interpretation Law`
#ASSERT `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word day` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1990 1 1) EQUALS `the definition in section 3 of the Interpretation Law`
#ASSERT `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) EQUALS `the definition in section 1 of the Interpretation Ordinance`
#ASSERT `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word month` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) EQUALS `the definition in section 1 of the Interpretation Ordinance`
#ASSERT `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word fiscal year` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) EQUALS `the definition in section 3 of the Interpretation Law`
#ASSERT `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word מימי חופין` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) EQUALS `the definition in section 3 of the Interpretation Law`
#ASSERT `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word פשע` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) EQUALS `the definition in section 3 of the Interpretation Law`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — the definition that governs` `the word day` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) BECAUSE "the Ordinance text defines no day: the Law's s 3 does not reach a word in an enactment given before the Law, and the Ordinance has no entry for it"

-- The calendar of a year or month: s 3 for a later enactment, the Ordinance (Gregorian, no Hebrew clause) for an earlier one.
#ASSERT `s 1, s 3, Ordinance s 1 — the calendar of a year or month in an enactment given on` (YMD 1990 1 1) `, for a period specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the Hebrew calendar`
#ASSERT `s 1, s 3, Ordinance s 1 — the calendar of a year or month in an enactment given on` (YMD 1990 1 1) `, for a period specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Gregorian calendar`
#ASSERT `s 1, s 3, Ordinance s 1 — the calendar of a year or month in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) `, for a period specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the Gregorian calendar`
#ASSERT `s 1, s 3, Ordinance s 1 — the calendar of a year or month in an enactment given on` (YMD 1960 5 1) `, for a period specified as` (`Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the Gregorian calendar`

§§ `Law s 20: an act imposed on several persons`

#ASSERT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 3 `of them did it`
#ASSERT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 3 `persons was validly done when` 2 `of them did it`
#ASSERT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 4 `persons was validly done when` 3 `of them did it`
#ASSERT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 1 `persons was validly done when` 1 `of them did it`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 2 `of them did it`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 4 `persons was validly done when` 2 `of them did it`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 2 `persons was validly done when` 1 `of them did it`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — an act imposed on` 1 `persons was validly done when` 0 `of them did it`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — an act imposed on` 3 `persons was validly done when` 5 `of them did it` BECAUSE "s 20 speaks of an act imposed on several persons and done by some of them; the numbers given do not fit that"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — an act imposed on` 0 `persons was validly done when` 0 `of them did it` BECAUSE "s 20 speaks of an act imposed on several persons and done by some of them; the numbers given do not fit that"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 20 — an act imposed on` 5 `persons was validly done when` 2.5 `of them did it` BECAUSE "s 20 speaks of an act imposed on several persons and done by some of them; the numbers given do not fit that"

§§ `Law s 22(2): a repeal cannot reach an earlier act`

-- A repeal commencing on 2026-03-01 binds from 00:01 on that day (s 21).
#ASSERT `s 22(2) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is powerless to affect an act done at` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 2 28) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59)
#ASSERT `s 22(2) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is powerless to affect an act done at` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is powerless to affect an act done at` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is powerless to affect an act done at` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2) — a repeal commencing on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is powerless to affect an act done at` (`the moment on` (YMD 2026 3 2) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 0)

§§ `Law s 23: regulations and appointments made under a repealed enactment`

#ASSERT `s 23 — the regulations and appointments made under a repealed enactment, where the repealing enactment provides provisions in their place:` TRUE EQUALS `they stand until they are cancelled by regulations and appointments under the repealing enactment`
#ASSERT `s 23 — the regulations and appointments made under a repealed enactment, where the repealing enactment provides provisions in their place:` FALSE EQUALS `they lapse with the repealed enactment`

§§ `Law s 24: the binding text`

#ASSERT `s 24 — the binding text of an enactment:` (`The text of an enactment` WITH `given in English before the State was established` IS TRUE, `a new text was fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the new text fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance`
#ASSERT `s 24 — the binding text of an enactment:` (`The text of an enactment` WITH `given in English before the State was established` IS TRUE, `a new text was fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the text in the language in which the enactment was given`
#ASSERT `s 24 — the binding text of an enactment:` (`The text of an enactment` WITH `given in English before the State was established` IS FALSE, `a new text was fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance` IS TRUE) EQUALS `the text in the language in which the enactment was given`
#ASSERT `s 24 — the binding text of an enactment:` (`The text of an enactment` WITH `given in English before the State was established` IS FALSE, `a new text was fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance` IS FALSE) EQUALS `the text in the language in which the enactment was given`

§§ `Law s 26: deviation from a form`

#ASSERT NOT `s 26 — the deviation disqualifies what was done under the form:` (`A deviation from a form fixed in an enactment` WITH `slight` IS TRUE, `harms the essential` IS FALSE, `misleads` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 26 — the deviation disqualifies what was done under the form:` (`A deviation from a form fixed in an enactment` WITH `slight` IS FALSE, `harms the essential` IS FALSE, `misleads` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 26 — the deviation disqualifies what was done under the form:` (`A deviation from a form fixed in an enactment` WITH `slight` IS TRUE, `harms the essential` IS TRUE, `misleads` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 26 — the deviation disqualifies what was done under the form:` (`A deviation from a form fixed in an enactment` WITH `slight` IS TRUE, `harms the essential` IS FALSE, `misleads` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 26 — the deviation disqualifies what was done under the form:` (`A deviation from a form fixed in an enactment` WITH `slight` IS FALSE, `harms the essential` IS TRUE, `misleads` IS TRUE)

§§ `Law s 31: what is left of the Ordinance`

#ASSERT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 16 `, subsection` (JUST 2) `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 16 `, subsection` (JUST 4) `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 16 `, subsection` (JUST 1) `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 16 `, subsection` (JUST 3) `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 16 `, subsection` (JUST 5) `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 17 `, subsection` NOTHING `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 19 `, subsection` NOTHING `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 42 `, subsection` NOTHING `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 1 `, subsection` NOTHING `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 10 `, subsection` NOTHING `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 43 `, subsection` NOTHING `, survives the Law`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` 16 `, subsection` NOTHING `, survives the Law` BECAUSE "s 31 saves subsections (2) and (4) of section 16 of the Ordinance but not the section as a whole, so a question about the whole section has no single answer"

§§ `Law s 33: publication within thirty days of adoption`

-- Thirty days from the day of adoption, 1981-05-20: May 20 is not counted, May 21 .. May 31 is 11 days, June 1 .. June 19 is 19.
#ASSERT `the day the Knesset adopted the Interpretation Law` EQUALS YMD 1981 5 20
#ASSERT (`s 33 — the last day for publishing a law adopted by the Knesset on` (YMD 1981 5 20)) EQUALS YMD 1981 6 19
#ASSERT (`s 33 — the last day for publishing a law adopted by the Knesset on` `the day the Knesset adopted the Interpretation Law`) EQUALS YMD 1981 6 19
#ASSERT (`s 33 — the last day for publishing a law adopted by the Knesset on` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 8, s 10 — the date` (YMD 1981 6 19) `is inside the period beginning on` (YMD 1981 5 21) `and ending on` (`s 33 — the last day for publishing a law adopted by the Knesset on` (YMD 1981 5 20))
#ASSERT NOT `s 8, s 10 — the date` (YMD 1981 6 20) `is inside the period beginning on` (YMD 1981 5 21) `and ending on` (`s 33 — the last day for publishing a law adopted by the Knesset on` (YMD 1981 5 20))

§§ `Ordinance s 16(4): a regulation may not contradict a law`

#ASSERT `Ordinance s 16(4) — s 16(4) forbids the regulation:` (`A regulation measured against s 16(4) of the Ordinance` WITH `the power to make it was conferred by a law` IS TRUE, `it contradicts a provision of a law` IS TRUE, `another intention is implied` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 16(4) — s 16(4) forbids the regulation:` (`A regulation measured against s 16(4) of the Ordinance` WITH `the power to make it was conferred by a law` IS TRUE, `it contradicts a provision of a law` IS FALSE, `another intention is implied` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 16(4) — s 16(4) forbids the regulation:` (`A regulation measured against s 16(4) of the Ordinance` WITH `the power to make it was conferred by a law` IS TRUE, `it contradicts a provision of a law` IS TRUE, `another intention is implied` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 16(4) — s 16(4) forbids the regulation:` (`A regulation measured against s 16(4) of the Ordinance` WITH `the power to make it was conferred by a law` IS FALSE, `it contradicts a provision of a law` IS TRUE, `another intention is implied` IS FALSE)

§§ `Ordinance s 19: using a power before the enactment commences`

`a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` MEANS `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement` WITH
    `the day the enactment was given` IS YMD 2026 1 10
    `the day the enactment commences` IS YMD 2026 7 1
    `using the power seems necessary or proper to operate the enactment on its commencement day` IS TRUE
    `another intention is implied` IS FALSE

`a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July, whose use is not needed` MEANS `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement` WITH
    `the day the enactment was given` IS YMD 2026 1 10
    `the day the enactment commences` IS YMD 2026 7 1
    `using the power seems necessary or proper to operate the enactment on its commencement day` IS FALSE
    `another intention is implied` IS FALSE

`a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July, with another intention implied` MEANS `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement` WITH
    `the day the enactment was given` IS YMD 2026 1 10
    `the day the enactment commences` IS YMD 2026 7 1
    `using the power seems necessary or proper to operate the enactment on its commencement day` IS TRUE
    `another intention is implied` IS TRUE

`a power that commences with its giving` MEANS `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement` WITH
    `the day the enactment was given` IS YMD 2026 1 10
    `the day the enactment commences` IS YMD 2026 1 10
    `using the power seems necessary or proper to operate the enactment on its commencement day` IS TRUE
    `another intention is implied` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `on` (YMD 2026 1 9)
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `on` (YMD 2026 1 10)
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `on` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July, whose use is not needed` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July, with another intention implied` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` `a power that commences with its giving` `on` (YMD 2026 1 10)

-- What was done under the power is not valid before the commencement day, unless it was needed to operate the
-- enactment or another intention is implied.
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 19 — the earliest day a regulation made under the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `may be valid, when it was needed to operate the enactment:` FALSE EQUALS `not before the day the enactment commences` (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 19 — the earliest day a regulation made under the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July` `may be valid, when it was needed to operate the enactment:` TRUE EQUALS `s 19 sets no earliest day`
#ASSERT `Ordinance s 19 — the earliest day a regulation made under the power of` `a power given 10 January, commencing 1 July, with another intention implied` `may be valid, when it was needed to operate the enactment:` FALSE EQUALS `s 19 sets no earliest day`

§§ `Ordinance s 42: the rights of the State`

#ASSERT `Ordinance s 42 — the enactment derogates from a right of the State or imposes a duty on it:` (`An enactment's effect on the State` WITH `it would derogate from a right of the State or impose a duty on it` IS TRUE, `it says so expressly` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 42 — the enactment derogates from a right of the State or imposes a duty on it:` (`An enactment's effect on the State` WITH `it would derogate from a right of the State or impose a duty on it` IS TRUE, `it says so expressly` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 42 — the enactment derogates from a right of the State or imposes a duty on it:` (`An enactment's effect on the State` WITH `it would derogate from a right of the State or impose a duty on it` IS FALSE, `it says so expressly` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Ordinance s 42 — the enactment derogates from a right of the State or imposes a duty on it:` (`An enactment's effect on the State` WITH `it would derogate from a right of the State or impose a duty on it` IS FALSE, `it says so expressly` IS FALSE)
